3. No selling

You may not Charge for:
  (a) the Work or any standalone copy of it;
  (b) a Modified Version;
  (c) any product or service where the Work is the main thing being offered;
      or
  (d) any add-on, plugin, extension or companion product whose main purpose
      is to work with, extend or unlock the Work.

This section does not restrict earning revenue from videos, streams,
reviews, articles or other commentary in which the Work is the subject being
shown, played, reviewed or discussed, as long as the Work itself is not made
available to obtain through them.

This section does not apply to physical goods.

4. Larger Works

Notwithstanding Section 3, you may include the Work in a Larger Work that you
Charge for, provided that:
  (a) the Larger Work would still be reasonably worth paying for with the
      Work, and every other work licensed under any version of this license,
      removed;
  (b) the Work is not presented as a main reason to buy, including in
      marketing, store listings or screenshots; and
  (c) users of the Larger Work are told where to get the Work free.
The parts of the Larger Work that come from the Work remain under this
license.

Using the Work, or any part of it, as music, sound, footage or artwork in a
video, stream, broadcast or recording that is not about the Work does not
qualify under this section. If that content earns revenue of any kind, it is
Charging.

A Larger Work may not Charge separately for installing, setting up, accessing,
supporting, customizing or unlocking the Work itself, or any part or feature
of it.

